# Monorepo Setup, Teardown & Troubleshooting

All commands run from the **monorepo root** unless noted otherwise.

## Node.js Version Management

**Required:** Node.js >= 22.22.0 (`.nvmrc`: `22.22.0`), pnpm 11.20.0.

Before running any `node`, `pnpm`, or `make` command, ensure the correct Node version is active. The user may use **nvm**, **nvs**, or **asdf**:

```bash
# nvm (most common)
export NVM_DIR="$HOME/.nvm"
[ -s "$NVM_DIR/nvm.sh" ] && . "$NVM_DIR/nvm.sh" && nvm use

# nvs
export NVS_HOME="$HOME/.nvs"
[ -s "$NVS_HOME/nvs.sh" ] && . "$NVS_HOME/nvs.sh" && nvs use auto

# asdf
[ -s "$HOME/.asdf/asdf.sh" ] && . "$HOME/.asdf/asdf.sh"
```

If `node --version` already shows a valid version, skip sourcing. Always verify before running shell commands.

## Python Version

Robot-stack Python projects use **Python 3.12** (`OT_VIRTUALENV_VERSION` in `scripts/python.mk`). The `OT_PYTHON` env var (default: `python`) selects the interpreter.

Standalone Python projects (`opentrons-ai-server/`, `e2e-testing/`, `analyses-snapshot-testing/`, `scripts/static-deploy/`) use **uv** for dependency management instead of pipenv. See their dedicated rules for details.

## Root Makefile — Quick Reference

### Setup (install dependencies)

| Target          | Description                                             |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `make setup`    | Install all JS and Python dependencies                  |
| `make setup-js` | Setup all JS projects (pnpm install)                    |
| `make setup-py` | Setup all robot Python packages (pipenv/uv per project) |

### Teardown (uninstall dependencies)

| Target             | Description                                      |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `make teardown`    | Teardown Python then JS (order matters)          |
| `make teardown-js` | Clean JS build output, remove all `node_modules` |
| `make teardown-py` | Teardown all robot Python packages               |

### Clean (remove build artifacts only)

| Target          | Description                                                  |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `make clean`    | Clean JS and Python build output                             |
| `make clean-js` | Clean JS build output (includes `clean-ts`)                  |
| `make clean-py` | Clean Python build output                                    |
| `make clean-ts` | Remove TypeScript declaration output (`tsc --build --clean`) |

### Test

**Prefer scoped tests.** When changes are in a specific package or directory, run tests only for that area rather than the entire repo. This is faster and gives more relevant feedback.

```bash
# Best: run tests for just the files near your changes
pnpm vitest protocol-designer/src/step-forms/
make test-js-protocol-designer tests="src/step-forms/"

# For Python, run from the project directory
cd api && make test  # or: make -C api test
```

**Full-repo targets** (use only when changes span multiple packages):

| Target                   | Description                                                           |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `make test`              | Run all JS and Python tests                                           |
| `make test-js`           | Run all JS tests (Vitest)                                             |
| `make test-js-<project>` | Run tests for one JS project (e.g., `make test-js-protocol-designer`) |
| `make test-py`           | Run all robot Python tests (pytest)                                   |

Pass options: `make test-js-<project> tests="src/path" test_opts="--reporter=verbose"`

### Frontend Lint & Format — Always Use These Three

All frontend (TS/TSX/JS/CSS) lint and format commands run from the **monorepo root** via these three Make targets. Do not call ESLint, Prettier, or Stylelint directly.

```bash
make format-js    # Prettier auto-format (all TS/TSX/JS/MD/JSON)
make lint-js      # ESLint + Prettier check (run after format-js to confirm clean)
make lint-css     # Stylelint check for all CSS Modules
```

Run `format-js` first to auto-fix, then `lint-js` and `lint-css` to verify nothing remains.

### Lint & Type-Check (full reference)

| Target                            | Description                                  |
| --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| `make lint-js`                    | ESLint + Prettier check                      |
| `make lint-js-eslint`             | ESLint only                                  |
| `make lint-js-prettier`           | Prettier only                                |
| `make lint-css`                   | Stylelint all CSS                            |
| `make lint-json`                  | ESLint for JSON files                        |
| `make lint-py`                    | Lint all robot Python projects (ruff + mypy) |
| `make check-js` / `make build-ts` | TypeScript type-check (`tsc --build`)        |
| `make circular-dependencies-js`   | Check for circular imports (madge)           |

### Format (auto-fix, full reference)

| Target            | Description                               |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| `make format-js`  | Prettier auto-format                      |
| `make format-py`  | ruff format for all robot Python projects |
| `make format-css` | Stylelint auto-fix                        |

### opentrons-ai-server Lint & Format

`opentrons-ai-server/` is a standalone Python project with its own Makefile. Run from inside that directory:

```bash
make format   # ruff format + ruff check --fix + prettier for MD/JSON
make lint     # ruff format --check + ruff check + mypy
```

## Standalone Python Projects

These projects have their **own** `Makefile` and use **uv** (not pipenv). They are NOT covered by root `make setup-py` / `make teardown-py`:

| Project                   | Directory                    | Setup Command                                     |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| AI Server                 | `opentrons-ai-server/`       | `make setup` (runs `uv sync`)                     |
| E2E Testing               | `e2e-testing/`               | `make setup` (runs `uv sync`)                     |
| Analyses Snapshot Testing | `analyses-snapshot-testing/` | `make setup` (runs bootstrap script; Python 3.12) |
| Static Deploy             | `scripts/static-deploy/`     | `make setup` (runs `uv sync`)                     |

Run their setup from within their own directory.

## Troubleshooting

### Stale or Broken node_modules

```bash
make teardown-js && make setup-js
```

### Pnpm Cache Corruption

```bash
pnpm cache delete && make setup-js
```

### TypeScript Build Artifacts Out of Sync

```bash
make clean-ts    # remove declaration output
make build-ts    # rebuild
```

### Python Virtual Environment Issues

```bash
make teardown-py && make setup-py
```

For standalone uv projects, run `make teardown && make setup` from within that project's directory.

### Wrong Node Version

```bash
node --version   # should show v22.22.0+
```

If wrong, re-source the version manager (see Node.js section above) or install the correct version:

```bash
nvm install       # reads .nvmrc
# or
nvs add auto
# or
asdf install nodejs
```

### "Module not found" Errors in JS

Usually means `pnpm` hasn't been run:

```bash
make setup-js
```

If a specific package is missing, try:

```bash
make teardown-js && make setup-js
```

### Port Conflicts for Dev Servers

```bash
lsof -i :<port>          # find the process
kill -9 <pid>            # kill it
```

### Nuclear Option — Full Reset

When nothing else works, tear down and rebuild everything:

```bash
make teardown && make setup
```

This removes all `node_modules`, Python venvs, and build output, then reinstalls from scratch.
